Alas, what you say may be practically correct, but is logically wrong.=A0 A=
ll predicates must have all arguments in place.=A0 If we omit some at the s=
urface level, they have to be restored uniquely at some level before interp=
retation.=A0 At the moment, Lojban does not have a way of doing this.=A0 As=
 you note, following CLL, sometime there just isn't something for that slot=
 -- which means, of course, that we have the predicate wrong, if not the ot=
her places.=A0 On the other hand, when there is something there, we have no=
 clear way of saying what should go there: the obvious value (I suppose thi=
s is sorta {zo'e}) or the any value that makes the whole true (presumably {=
da}), but no rule as to which to pick (and {zo'e}'s use here does not fit w=
ell with its use in "definitions" of gadri).=A0=20




